Removes two `#[no_mangle]` attributes from casper-contract 5.1.1.

Why this is needed: current rustc rejects `#[no_mangle]` on internal language items
("`#[no_mangle]` cannot be used on internal language items"), and `#[panic_handler]` /
`#[alloc_error_handler]` are exactly that. Without this patch the crate — and therefore this
contract — does not compile at all on any recent toolchain. Verified 2026-07-25 on rustc 1.97.1.

The attributes are redundant anyway: rustc already requires these items to carry their specific
mangled names, so dropping `#[no_mangle]` changes no emitted symbol.

Apply with `prepare_patched_crate.sh` (or `patch -p1` from the crate root).

--- a/src/no_std_handlers.rs
+++ b/src/no_std_handlers.rs
@@ -2,7 +2,6 @@

 /// A panic handler for use in a `no_std` environment which simply aborts the process.
 #[panic_handler]
-#[no_mangle]
 pub fn panic(_info: &core::panic::PanicInfo) -> ! {
     #[cfg(feature = "test-support")]
     crate::contract_api::runtime::print(&alloc::format!("{_info}"));
@@ -12,7 +11,6 @@
 /// An out-of-memory allocation error handler for use in a `no_std` environment which simply aborts
 /// the process.
 #[alloc_error_handler]
-#[no_mangle]
 pub fn oom(_: core::alloc::Layout) -> ! {
     core::intrinsics::abort();
 }
